FixedRateIrm::constructor(uint256,address)
├── given owner is zero even when the borrow rate is also invalid
│   └── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner before validating the rate
└── given owner is nonzero
    ├── when borrow rate exceeds MAX_BORROW_RATE
    │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    └── when borrow rate is valid
        ├── when rate is zero or MAX_BORROW_RATE
        │   └── it should accept both inclusive boundaries
        ├── when rate is any value inside the supported range
        │   └── it should store the supplied rate exactly
        ├── it should set owner and leave pendingOwner and market zero
        ├── it should initialize lastUpdate to zero regardless of deployment time
        ├── it should emit OwnershipTransferred from zero to owner
        └── it should then emit exactly IRStateUpdated with the supplied rate and zero timestamp
